<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">2003</h1><p class="ref-lede">2003 in world history: 28 events, 9 deaths, 1 state founded and 1 that came to an end. 258 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1999">1999</a><a href="/years/2000">2000</a><a href="/years/2001">2001</a><a href="/years/2002">2002</a><a href="/years/2003" aria-current="page">2003</a><a href="/years/2004">2004</a><a href="/years/2005">2005</a><a href="/years/2006">2006</a><a href="/years/2007">2007</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-16">16 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Space Shuttle Columbia launches on its final mission</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Columbia lifted off on mission STS-107 with seven astronauts. Foam debris struck its wing during launch, and the shuttle broke apart on re-entry sixteen days later, killing the crew.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-1">1 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Space Shuttle Columbia breaks up on re-entry</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Columbia disintegrated over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> minutes before landing, killing all seven astronauts. Hot gases had entered a wing damaged by foam at launch; shuttle flights were suspended for two and a half years.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-9">9 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Baghdad falls and Saddam's statue is pulled down</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">As US troops entered central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>, a statue of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saddam-hussein">Saddam Hussein</a> in Firdos Square was toppled with the help of a Marine vehicle. The images marked the regime's collapse, though years of insurgency followed.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-1">1 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">George W. Bush declares major combat in Iraq over</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Speaking aboard USS <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abraham-lincoln">Abraham Lincoln</a> beneath a 'Mission Accomplished' banner, the president announced the end of major combat operations. The insurgency that followed made the moment notorious.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-24">24 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Concorde makes its last commercial flight</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">British Airways Concorde flight BA002 from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> landed at Heathrow, ending 27 years of supersonic passenger travel. The aircraft could cross the Atlantic in about three and a half hours.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/rose-revolution" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rose-revolution.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolution</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/rose-revolution">Rose Revolution</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Rose Revolution was the peaceful change of power in Georgia in November 2003.</p></div></li></ol></section>
