<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/language/nahuatl"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Nahuatl.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Nahuatl</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Mexico’s law on linguistic rights recognises Nahuatl and other Indigenous languages as national languages</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-mapungubwe"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Mapungubwe.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Mapungubwe</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Mapungubwe Cultural Landscape becomes a UNESCO World Heritage Site</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/lapita-culture"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Lapita%20culture.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Lapita culture</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Lapita cemetery at Teouma on Efate, Vanuatu, is discovered</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/kerma-culture"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kerma%20culture.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kerma culture</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Charles Bonnet’s Swiss team finds a cache of granite statues of the Twenty-fifth Dynasty pharaohs at Kerma</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/azerbaijan"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Azerbaijan.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Azerbaijan</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Ilham Aliyev succeeds his father Heydar as President and chairman of the New Azerbaijan Party.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/georgia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Georgia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Georgia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Rose Revolution led by Mikheil Saakashvili, Zurab Zhvania and Nino Burjanadze deposes Shevardnadze after the fraudulent elections of 2 November.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/san-people"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/San%20people.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>San people</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The San win a benefit-sharing agreement over their knowledge of the hoodia plant, and their representatives ask to be called by their own nations’ names</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/haitian-vodou"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Haitian%20Vodou.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Haitian Vodou</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">President Jean-Bertrand Aristide grants Vodou official recognition, after the constitution of 1987 enshrined freedom of religion</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/peronism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Peronism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Peronism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Néstor Kirchner wins the presidency and returns the movement to Perón’s left-wing populism</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/epic-of-gilgamesh"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Epic%20of%20Gilgamesh.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Epic of Gilgamesh</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Andrew George publishes his two-volume critical edition with Oxford University Press</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/terracotta-army"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Terracotta%20Army.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Terracotta Army</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A grave pit holding 121 skeletons attributed to the site’s workers is excavated</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/rosetta-stone"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Rosetta%20Stone.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Rosetta Stone</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Zahi Hawass called for the stone to be returned to Egypt</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/federal-republic-of-yugoslavia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Federal%20Republic%20of%20Yugoslavia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Federal Republic of Yugoslavia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Constitutional Charter turns the federation into the State Union of Serbia and Montenegro</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/the-republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/The%20Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>The Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Simon R. Slings publishes a new Oxford edition of the Greek text</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/palace-of-versailles"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Palace%20of%20Versailles.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Palace of Versailles</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Grand Versailles restoration project began with the replanting of the gardens</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/declaration-of-the-rights-of-man-and-of-the-citizen"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Declaration%20of%20the%20Rights%20of%20Man%20and%20of%20the%20Citizen.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Declaration of the Rights of Man and of the Citizen</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">UNESCO adds the 1789 version, the first printed one, to its Memory of the World International Register</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/baathism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ba'athism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ba'athism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The invasion of Iraq topples Saddam Hussein, and the Iraqi Ba'ath party is banned</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/mandaeism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mandaeism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mandaeism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Many Mandaeans flee Iraq after the invasion and the rise in sectarian violence by extremists; by 2007 about 5,000 remain</span></li></ul></section>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Wars and longer events</h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/iraq-war"><span class="ph ph-event" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Iraq War</span><span class="tp">Began · 2003–2011</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/united-nations-mission-in-liberia"><span class="ph ph-conflict" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">United Nations Mission in Liberia</span><span class="tp">Began · 2003–2018</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/human-genome-project"><span class="ph ph-event" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Human Genome Project</span><span class="tp">Ended · 1990–2003</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/second-congo-war"><span class="ph ph-event" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Second Congo War</span><span class="tp">Ended · 1998–2003</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
